      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-06-15_WidnesExaminer_art0051" n="art0051">
        <head>CHANGEABLE WEATHER.</head>
        <p>THE CHANGEABLE WEATHER.</p>
        <p>The fickle nature of the climate of this country often gives rise to a variety of ailments and complaints, which tssuming at first the form of only a slight indispo:ition f neglected and unheeded may become the germ of ,erious diseases, which will undermine the constitution, %nd finally result in a long and lingering illness, and oerhaps termieate fatally. The variable temperature and tee changeable weather of the last month or so. makes it inc-ambent on all of us to exercise wise and pru. epee precautions to counteract the evil effects which the weather may have had upon our health and comfort. Already we frequently hear such complaints as " No appetite,"" These frequent headaches," •"I'his languid feeling," and dczens of other expressions which all point to the urgent need of a good Tonic. Now there are several tonic mixtures offered to tt,e Public, but none which have been so uniformly successful al Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, The Vegetable Tonic. This pre- paration is acknowledged to be The Best Remedy of The Age for Nervousness, Weakness, Cbest Affections, Palpi- tation of the Heart, Indigestion, s Liver Consp‘aint and lefluenza. The numerous cases of marvellous cures effected, and the restoration to perfect health, of those who had lone suffered and bad vainly tried other remedies, can be Recounted for by simply stating the effect which Cr wilym Evans' Quinine Bitters has upon the System. Ist. It strikes at the source of the disease, and by removing the causes of disease, the evil effects soon vanish. 2ad. It strengthens that part of the system which is weakest, and therefore, most liable to the attacks of colds and all diseases. 3rd. It purifies the blood, and this gives new life ad force to all parts of the body, for disease can- not exist where there is a free circulation of pure blood. 4th. It gives healthy action to the digestive organs, ' and to the liver, thus aiding to keep away Indigestion. and the host of different forms of disease which result from it. sth. By removing impuritiea, strengthenicg the weak parts of the system, and purifying the blood, the human frame is well fortified to withstand the attacks of disease. It is repelled, and its place taken by health and strength, through the effective action of Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, The Vegetable Tonic. Sold everywhere in bottles, 2s. 9d. and 4s. 61. each, or will be sent carriage free for these prices, direct from the Sole Proprietors :—Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Company, Limited, Llanelly, South Wales. Beware of imitations. See that you get the genuine Preparation with the came" Gwilym Evans "on Label, Stamp, and Bottle without which Irene is genuine.</p>
