      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-06-15_WidnesExaminer_art0100" n="art0100">
        <head>--4•-•-., Gospel Hall.</head>
        <p>--4•-•-., Gospel Hall.</p>
        <p>On Sunday, Mr. W. French, of Manchester, conducted the service, pro/china from the story in Luke 19-nO, " tochens, the Publican." affirming that the greatest sinne:s often make the brightest saints when saved, as inetanc,d in the cases of John Bunyan, Richard Weaver and others. Jericho, the city which Crld had cursed. had a large number of priests and a large num- hcr of publicans resident there. The Jews deipised and lenked down upon the publicans or taxgatherers and Z Accheus was chief of this &amp;ass. Re sought to see Jesus but he got more than he expected for Christ received him though the chief of sinners and he received Christ and thus a work was done which brought Zaccheus salvation and it was to him a happy day. Some think the lot of a Christian gloomy but all true Christians testify that lasting happiness is only to be found in Christ.</p>
