Haydock On Saturday. Score : moss BANK. lIATDOCK. Y C Davies (captain) It Yates l4 J Boardman l5 J Yates 8 W Smith C Midd jun l5 II Smith W Mida 5 5 Valentine l5 T Midd W Yates B Taylor M Mtdd l2 J Malone l5 W H Midd F Sephton J Gaskell . Th.ts. Ashcroft 9 W E Pimblett H Fairciough W F Macdonald 3 5 Davits P Frodsham C Taylor 178 23 Majority for Haydock 57 FOOTBALL. The Northern Union. Meeting at Huddersfield. On Tuesday night, a meeting of the committee was held at the George Hotel, Huddersfield, Mr. J. a. Smith, Widnes, in the chair.—lt was resolved that the Dalton Club be ordered to pay the Barrow St. Geor,--e's Club 30s for broken engagement on Good Friday.—The following clubs were admitted to membership: Otley, Bingley, Keighley, and Aspatria.-llr Kilnor. s-cretary of the Oldham Club, reported A Hall, of that club, for playing football whilst out of employment. Toe committee decided that the Oldham Club be exonerated from blame seeing that Hall hid failed to notify the Oldham Club that be was not working, and that Hall be suspended up to and includ- ing October 31st.—On an application from the Cheshire County Union for financial .ssistance, the Committee decided to grant a sum of £5O to each County in the union.—lt was resolved that £lOO be devoted to the Broughton Rangers Club in consideration of the fact of the venue of the final tie in the Union Cup competition being removed to Fallowfield.—Riasolved that the Swin- ton Club be allowed to present four extra medals, as desired,in commemoration of their winning the Northern Union cup.—Resolved, that the alterations of rules sug- geAed by Cumberland Senior Competition, namely, the inclease of subscription from 10) 6d to a guinea, and I substituting 3.15 p.m. for 3 o clock as the time of kick I off, be canfirtned.—The consideration of the Committee's I suggested alterations of rules was adjourned till Monday.</p>
